  "guid": "com.icyclawz.itemattributefix",
  "name": "Item Attribute Fix",
  "slug": "item-attribute-fix",
  "teaser": "A universal fix for item attribute tooltip not being updated when the attribute has changed while the inspection window is open.",
  "thumbnail": "https://forge-static.sp-tarkov.com/mods/1232.png",
  "downloads": 20882,
  "favourites_count": 26,
  "description": "<p><strong>Installation:</strong></p>\n<p>Extract the ZIP to your SPT-AKI installation folder.</p>\n<p><strong>Description:</strong></p>\n<p>The tooltip shown when hovering over an attribute in the item inspection window is static by default.</p>\n<p>In order to update it after an item has been changed (e.g. ammo added to a magazine, mods attached/detached to/from gear, etc.), the inspection window has to be closed and reopened.</p>\n<p>This simple client-side mod updates the tooltip’s text the moment the attribute is being updated.</p>\n<p>This fix can be used with any mod that utilizes the attribute tooltips (“FullStringValue” field of “ItemAttributeClass”).</p>\n<p>This fix was initially made as a companion to my “<a target=\"_blank\" class=\"external-link\" href=\"https://forge.sp-tarkov.com/mod/909/item-sell-price\" rel=\"noreferrer noopener\">Item Sell Price</a>” and “<a target=\"_blank\" class=\"external-link\" href=\"https://forge.sp-tarkov.com/mod/914/magazine-inspector\" rel=\"noreferrer noopener\">Magazine Inspector</a>” mods.</p>\n",
  "detail_url": "https://forge.sp-tarkov.com/mod/910/item-attribute-fix",
